#
# The sign-in stack of the Appliance Console on an rpm host (AlmaLinux), installed at
# /etc/pam.d/olivares-portal by the rpm. The deb installs ../olivares-portal instead; its header
# states why the file exists, why the group check is first and requisite, why the session and
# password groups are denied, and what was measured against a real stack, and all
# of it holds here. This is the same stack over AlmaLinux's scheme: password-auth, the stack
# authselect generates for services a human reaches over the network, which AlmaLinux's own sshd
# includes. AlmaLinux has no common-auth or common-account, and an include of a file the host does
# not have fails the whole stack.
#
# On AlmaLinux a service with no file of its own gets the "other" stack, which denies every
# group, so an absent file admits nobody there. The console still treats absence as unusable,
# the same on every host.
auth       requisite   pam_succeed_if.so user ingroup olivares-admins
auth       include     password-auth
account    required    pam_succeed_if.so user ingroup olivares-admins
account    include     password-auth
password   required    pam_deny.so
session    required    pam_deny.so
